          {
            "id": 2752866,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Today, we continue our series on ecology and conservation with a look at a particularly endangered member of the black bear family. One in ten black bears is actually born with a white coat, which is the result of a special gene that surfaces in a few. Local people have named it the spirit bear, and according to the legends of these communities, its snowy fur brings with it a special power. Because of this, it has always been highly regarded by them so much that they do not speak of seeing it to anyone else. It is their way of protecting it when strangers visit the area.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2752867,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Today, we continue our series on ecology and conservation with a look at a particularly endangered member of the black bear family.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 108.435,
                  "from": 98.035,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2752890,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "One in ten black bears is actually born with a white coat, which is the result of a special gene that surfaces in a few.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 118.6,
                  "from": 108.915,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2752916,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Local people have named it the spirit bear, and according to the legends of these communities, its snowy fur brings with it a special power.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 130.05501,
                  "from": 119.4,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2752942,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Because of this, it has always been highly regarded by them so much that they do not speak of seeing it to anyone else.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 140.13501,
                  "from": 130.855,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2752967,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "It is their way of protecting it when strangers visit the area.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 145.15001,
                  "from": 140.75,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2752980,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "The white bear's habitat is quite interesting. The bear's strong relationship with the old growth rainforest is a complex one. The white bear relies on the huge centuries old trees in the forest in many ways. For example, the old growth trees have extremely long roots that help prevent erosion of the soil along the banks of the many fish streams. Keeping these banks intact is important because these streams are home to salmon, which are the bear's main food source.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2752981,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The white bear's habitat is quite interesting.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 149.07,
                  "from": 146.11,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2752989,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The bear's strong relationship with the old growth rainforest is a complex one.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 155.31,
                  "from": 149.63,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2753003,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "The white bear relies on the huge centuries old trees in the forest in many ways.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 162.835,
                  "from": 156.195,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2753020,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "For example, the old growth trees have extremely long roots that help prevent erosion of the soil along the banks of the many fish streams.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 173.78,
                  "from": 163.55501,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2753046,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Keeping these banks intact is important because these streams are home to salmon, which are the bear's main food source.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 182.18,
                  "from": 174.34,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2753067,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "In return, the bear's feeding habits nurture the forest. As the bears eat the salmon, they discard the skin and bones in great amounts on the forest floor, which provide vital nutrients. These produce lush vegetation that sustains thousands of other types of life forms from birds to insects and more. Today, the spirit bear lives off the coast of the province of British Columbia on a few islands. There is great concern for their survival since it is estimated that less than 200 of these white bears remain.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2753068,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In return, the bear's feeding habits nurture the forest.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 188.125,
                  "from": 183.72499,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2753078,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "As the bears eat the salmon, they discard the skin and bones in great amounts on the forest floor, which provide vital nutrients.",
